#
# holt — GraphQL for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract GraphQL symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `GraphQL`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own GraphQL parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"GraphQL\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### GraphQL ####################################################################
--langdef=HoltGraphQL
--map-HoltGraphQL=+.graphql
--map-HoltGraphQL=+.gql
--kinddef-HoltGraphQL=t,type,types
--kinddef-HoltGraphQL=f,field,operations
--regex-HoltGraphQL=/^[ \t]*(type|input|interface|enum|union|scalar|schema)[ \t]+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)/\2/t/
--regex-HoltGraphQL=/^[ \t]*(query|mutation|subscription|fragment)[ \t]+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)/\2/f/
